{"date":"2026-11-08","caps":[[0.05,"Arnie Jordan here, coming to you from row three at Jordan Arena, with the Rinkside Report."],[5.23,"Sunday, November eighth, and I came with a coffee and a brand new system. Two pens."],[10.02,"Blue pen for goals, red pen for the penalty box. My nephew says that's how the professionals do it."],[15.71,"My nephew is nine. Hold that thought."],[18.5,"The early game was The Keg Canucks against the ColdBreak Leafs."],[22.04,"Adams opened it four minutes in, and Steele made it two nothing thirty-four seconds later."],[27.08,"Then the Canucks answered with a genuine Short to Short connection. Wes Short set it up, Adam Short buried it."],[33.22,"Bowen tied it."],[34.05,"Then Larry Penney and Haroutunian scored forty-one seconds apart late in the first, and it was four to two Leafs."],[41.0,"The red pen got a workout too."],[42.6,"Adam Short went off for roughing in the first, and Wes Short went off for slashing in the second."],[47.67,"So the Shorts scored together and served together."],[50.31,"And Steele, who scored twice on the night, took three minutes for a slap shot."],[54.4,"In this league that's the one shot you are not allowed to take, and he took it anyway, like a fella ordering the one thing that's not on the menu."],[62.0,"The Plug came in for Rennie partway through the second, and nobody scored in the whole period."],[67.57,"Then the third, and the Canucks woke up."],[69.68,"Gates went off for tripping, and Colin Murphy scored on the power play, from Goodie and Beckett."],[74.67,"Steele got it back. Then Leyenhorst, then Goodie with three twenty-eight left, and it's five all."],[79.72,"The Leafs blew a two-goal lead three different times. Last week I kept a Leafs Lead Counter."],[84.51,"This week I kept a Leafs Lead Shredder."],[87.21,"Last two minutes, within two goals, so it's stop time, and the clock stops on every whistle."],[92.16,"Then Darren Horton, from Collini and Pierce, with thirty-six seconds left. Six to five Leafs."],[97.16,"The Canucks pulled The Plug for an extra skater and threw everything at the net, and none of it went in."],[102.75,"Rosie went the whole game in the Leafs net, which is more than you can say for any of their leads."],[108.67,"Game two, the Timbit Senators against the RegattaSport Nordiques, and the red pen had exactly one customer."],[114.56,"Dykstra. Two trips in the first period. While he sat for the second one, Williams scored on the power play."],[120.45,"One more and you're done for the night, Dykstra, so walk, don't skate."],[124.32,"He scored seventy seconds into the third, so that's a goal, two assists and two trips. A full itinerary."],[130.68,"Goals for the Nordiques from Brophy, Moorzey, Rob DeBolster, Whetlam, Lawrence, Dykstra and Langlois."],[136.43,"Seven different goal scorers, and it finished nine to four."],[139.81,"Moorzey had four points, and Regular had three assists, which for a fella named Regular is anything but."],[146.33,"For the Senators, Williams had a hat trick, one of them all by himself, and lost by five."],[151.08,"That's bringing a turkey to the potluck and finding out everybody else brought nine."],[155.56,"And Shannon went the whole game in the Senators net and watched nine go by."],[159.58,"Somebody get that man a rear-view mirror."],[162.43,"The late game, Dawson's Oilers against the J.E. Culp Habs."],[165.82,"Crandles went off for hooking twenty-seven seconds in, and Foran scored on the power play, from Craigy and Wall."],[172.32,"Abrams made it two nothing, from Brown and Grossi."],[175.25,"Then Grossi took three minutes for unsportsmanlike conduct, abuse of officials."],[179.85,"Grossi had something to say to the referee, and the referee had three minutes to say back."],[185.08,"Tuby got the Habs on the board late in the first, from KP and Dixon."],[189.69,"The second period was all Habs. Hunt, KP, Clark and Jim Culp. Five in a row, five to two."],[195.02,"Right as Culp's went in, the Oilers swapped Raimondo out for Dawson, and I knocked my coffee onto the blue page."],[201.7,"So the blue page is now a brown page."],[204.59,"And then the Habs stopped scoring. Completely. Dawson didn't let in another goal all night."],[209.88,"Derrick DeBolster got one back, from HoundDog and Craigy, and McPherson made it five to four, from Grossi."],[216.04,"Then Greg Penney went off for hooking, and Craigy tied it, from Mansion, five seconds after Penney's penalty ran out."],[222.83,"Five seconds. Penney barely had time to close the penalty box door behind him."],[228.02,"Down the other end, Levar took at least three pucks right off the face mask."],[232.05,"I was starting to worry, and then I figured it out. The man was hungry."],[235.82,"Somebody told him the canteen had puck burgers on special, and he was trying to order through the cage."],[241.26,"Levar, buddy, they go in the glove."],[243.78,"Tied at the buzzer, so it's a shootout, and that's three weeks running. McPherson buried it."],[248.48,"Six to five Oilers. Habs, you scored five straight and went home with nothing."],[252.47,"Grossi, two assists and a talking-to."],[254.4,"Somewhere in that game, a pass went the whole width of the ice and straight out the bench door."],[259.25,"I didn't catch who threw it, and I'm not asking."],[262.37,"So that's your week: a Leafs Lead Shredder, a Short to Short connection, and a full itinerary for Dykstra."],[268.35,"The blue pen is out of ink, the red pen is fine, and the blue page is brown."],[272.66,"My nephew says next week we try crayons."],[274.96,"If I got your name wrong, or gave your goal to the fella beside you, take it up with the refs, the timekeeper, and how fast you guys skate out there."],[283.35,"Tape your sticks. This has been Arnie Jordan with the Rinkside Report."]],"kf":[{"t":18.5,"g":0,"per":"1","clk":1200,"h":0,"a":0,"goal":null,"final":false},{"t":22.04,"g":0,"per":"1","clk":939,"h":1,"a":0,"goal":"ADAMS","final":false},{"t":24.09,"g":0,"per":"1","clk":905,"h":2,"a":0